From: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 0019] misc: sdp-micom: add IR blaster/receiver and IR sender probe skeletons

Add DT nodes for the Samsung SDP Nike-L IR Blaster/Receiver (IRB) and
IR Sender (IRS) peripherals and their probe-only driver skeletons.

All register addresses and IRQ numbers come from the firmware DTB dtb0
(nikel-2G, sha256 0189cc94):

  /soc/mcirb  compatible "samsung,sdp-mc-irb"
              reg <0x9c1300 0x20>
              interrupts <0 0x6e 0>  = GIC SPI 110
              status "okay" (kept disabled in our DT for safety)

  /soc/mcirs  compatible "samsung,sdp-mc-irs"
              reg <0x9c1400 0x20>
              interrupts <0 0x6f 0>  = GIC SPI 111
              status "okay" (kept disabled in our DT for safety)

GPL source is available in the Samsung 20_DTV_NikeL package:
  drivers/misc/sdp_micom_irb.c  (335 lines)
  drivers/misc/sdp_micom_irs.c  (372 lines)

Full port deferred until a MODE=show runner run imports those sources.
The skeletons:
  - map the single MMIO region
  - register the IRQ (not used)
  - return 0 from probe

Built as CONFIG_SDP_MICOM_IRB=m and CONFIG_SDP_MICOM_IRS=m so they
never load on the TV.  DT nodes are status = "disabled".

Signed-off-by: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>
